E('insignificance','/ˌɪnsɪɡˈnɪfɪkəns/','不重要；微不足道；渺小','insignificance 把“不占多少分量”的状态当名词谈，像大山旁边的一粒石子。','in-（不）+ significance，英语否定派生。',D(SIGNIFICANCE,'in- + significance → insignificance','缺乏重要性、影响力的状态'),'pale into insignificance 是相比之下显得微不足道；a sense of insignificance 是觉得自己渺小。','pale into insignificance；a sense of insignificance；relative insignificance。','invisibility 是看不见；insignificance 是被认为不重要，不一定真的不显眼。',('Our earlier difficulties paled into insignificance beside the new crisis.','与新危机相比，先前的困难显得微不足道。'),('The vast landscape gave him a sense of his own insignificance.','广阔的景色让他感到自己的渺小。')),
